  "design": {
    "decision": "Buy [♦] cards and length-making enablers over honors, and bid knowing a [♦]-heavy hand both pays and is likely to be trumped.",
    "opponent": "Shown after bidding; opponents void [♦] early and trump it to set a team whose multiplier now cuts both ways.",
    "rationale": "Whole-hand counts measure well. This is the compounding top end of the [♦] length line: about ×1.9 at an average 6.5 [♦]s, and it grows with the cards and enablers a run buys. It works without enablers but rewards them, and a set hurts more.",
